#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2259 src/ubuntu_start.py:2267
msgid "Print job is stuck or the queue is paused"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2268
msgid "Check the printer itself"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2268
msgid ""
"Check its display or status lights, power, paper, open covers, and ink or "
"toner before sending the job again."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2269
msgid "Refresh the local queue"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2269
msgid ""
"Open Network and hardware and refresh Printer queue status. The queue state "
"and unfinished-job count can show whether work is waiting or the queue is "
"paused."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2270
msgid "Review the queue in Printer Settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2270
msgid ""
"Open Printer Settings and inspect the queue. Cancel only a job you own and "
"are ready to discard. On a shared printer, ask its owner or administrator "
"before changing other jobs."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2271
msgid "Send one test page"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2271
msgid ""
"After fixing the cause, send one test page. Avoid resending the same "
"document repeatedly if it does not print."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2273
msgid "Wi-Fi is slow or keeps disconnecting"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2274
msgid "Compare the connection near the router"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2274
msgid ""
"Move closer to the router and try the same task again. If it works better "
"nearby, distance or obstacles may be weakening the signal."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2275
msgid "Check the active Wi-Fi link"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2275
msgid ""
"Refresh Network status on the Network and hardware page. When available, "
"signal values closer to 0 dBm are stronger. Receive and transmit rates "
"describe the Wi-Fi link, not your measured internet speed."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2276
msgid "Compare another device or service"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2276
msgid ""
"Try another device on the same Wi-Fi and another app or website. If several "
"devices have trouble, check the router or ask your internet provider. If "
"only this computer is affected, check its adapter and Ubuntu updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2277
msgid "Look for nearby channel overlap"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2277
msgid ""
"The WiFi Analyzer recommendation on the Network and hardware page can help "
"you review nearby signal levels and channel use. It opens an external "
"project page after confirmation; ask the network owner before changing "
"router settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2278
msgid "Keep private details out of support requests"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2278
msgid ""
"Share the adapter model, hardware ID and driver if you need help. Do not "
"share the Wi-Fi password or private network details."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2282
msgid "Use Mouse Keys"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2283
msgid "Open Pointing & Clicking"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2283
msgid "In Accessibility Settings, open the Pointing & Clicking section."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2284
msgid "Turn on Mouse Keys"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2284
msgid ""
"Mouse Keys lets you control the pointer with the numeric keypad. Turn Num "
"Lock off to use the keypad for pointer movement."
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2285
msgid "Test it and turn it off if needed"
msgstr ""

#: src/ubuntu_start.py:2285
msgid ""
"Try moving the pointer and clicking a simple target. Return to Pointing & "
"Clicking to turn Mouse Keys off when you are finished."
msgstr ""

